Description: end the volume walk on B_INVALID_DEV, not on a sign test
 dev_t is unsigned here, so ">= B_OK" is always true and the index
 setup walked the volume list forever, leaving the window unshown and
 the app deaf to its quit message. Compare with B_INVALID_DEV, which
 next_dev() returns at the end of the list.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/src/db/QueryDBManager.cpp
+++ b/src/db/QueryDBManager.cpp
@@ -876,7 +876,7 @@
 	int32 cookie = 0;
 	dev_t device;
 
-	while ((device = next_dev(&cookie)) >= B_OK) {
+	while ((device = next_dev(&cookie)) != B_INVALID_DEV) {
 		fs_info info;
 		if (fs_stat_dev(device, &info) < 0
 			|| (info.flags & B_FS_HAS_QUERY) == 0)
